        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Frederick Lindemann, 1st Viscount Cherwell; Winston Churchill\n- Roles: British government's chief scientific adviser; British Prime Minister\n- Documents: dehousing paper; memorandum\n- Concepts: dehousing\n\nFacts:\n- Frederick Alexander Lindemann, 1st Viscount Cherwell, lived from 5 April 1886 to 3 July 1957.\n- Frederick Lindemann was a British physicist and an influential scientific adviser to the British government from the early 1940s to the early 1950s.\n- Frederick Lindemann particularly advised Winston Churchill during that period.\n- On 30 March 1942, Professor Frederick Lindemann, Baron Cherwell, was the British government's chief scientific adviser.\n- On 30 March 1942, Frederick Lindemann sent British Prime Minister Winston Churchill a memorandum.\n- After the British Cabinet accepted that memorandum, the document became known as the dehousing paper.",
